    "notes": "Reviewed approximate fit on the retained unchanged161-square/6m standard DEM. Low wall crests, stone bases and timber-post foundations follow local terrain samples, with buried sides below grade. The planar solar slab is conservatively above its sampled coarse-terrain envelope after its initial half-buried draft was corrected; its exact ancient threshold is not claimed. No ground or water cutout.24 mapped ancient records are replaced to numerical boundary remnants below1e-7m² per record, preserving both open fort interiors and both independent modern ticket/ranger buildings byte-for-byte. Failed loading restores all26 native map records; eviction releases geometry. The source-local PNG is a16-bit encoding of this same retained grid for visual review, not a new terrain survey. Model+X is east,+Z south at heading0. Rectangular shrine axes follow actual mapped edges; circles have no facade azimuth.24 source controls retain their original polygons/holes. The broad old fortress axis is not reused as a shrine direction. Named solar POI and mapped circular lobe differ by about6m; the lobe/channel geometry controls this visualization. Disc radius and post/base counts are picture-led estimates."
