    "notes": "Accepted as medium-fi surviving exterior and approximate standard-map fit. Timber posts represent the modern reconstruction, not ancient surviving wood. Exact original sanctuary design, current post/base inventory, damage patterns and excavated terrace grades are not surveyed. Both wall circuits follow the mapped traces; the source photograph guides surviving low gray stone, despite coarse wood/building tags. Forest, furnishings and full ancient buildings are outside this structural asset. The tilted planar solar slab and terrain-following foundations fit coarse data rather than exact archaeological floors. Far walls are crest surfaces because their height is subpixel at their intended distance."
